.TH UNPACK 1 "August 2026" "pack-unpack 1.6.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
unpack \- automatically unpack compressed archives
.PP
Optional compatibility alias:
.BR extract (1)
(symlink to unpack; omit on systems where GNU libextractor owns
.BR /usr/bin/extract ).
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B unpack
.B \-\-version
.br
.B unpack
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.br
.B unpack
.RB [ \-v | \-\-verbose ]
.RB [ \-p | \-\-preserve ]
.RB [ \-C
.IR dir ]
.RB [ \-f | \-n | \-i ]
.RB [ \-\- ]
.I archive
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B unpack
opens
.I archive
with
.BR libarchive (3)
(all supported formats and filters) and writes members into the current
directory (or into
.I dir
when
.B \-C
is given). On success
.B unpack
is silent. Use
.B \-v
to list member paths as they are unpacked.
.PP
By default, extraction restores file content, directory structure, symlinks,
hardlinks, and modification times under the process umask. Absolute member
paths,
.B ..
components, and unsafe hardlink targets are rejected. Extraction enables
.BR ARCHIVE_EXTRACT_SECURE_SYMLINKS ,
.BR ARCHIVE_EXTRACT_SECURE_NODOTDOT ,
.BR ARCHIVE_EXTRACT_SECURE_NOABSOLUTEPATHS ,
and
.B ARCHIVE_EXTRACT_SAFE_WRITES .
Default and
.B \-n
modes also set
.BR ARCHIVE_EXTRACT_NO_OVERWRITE .
Pass
.B \-p
to restore full permission bits, ACLs, and file flags.
.PP
After all members are written,
.B archive_write_close
is checked so deferred directory metadata failures are not reported as success.
.PP
Default overwrite policy: if a member path already exists,
.B unpack
asks whether to overwrite
.RB ( y / N )
when stdin and stderr are a tty; otherwise a conflict aborts with an error.
Answer
.B n
(or Enter) to skip that member.
.B Ctrl+C
cancels the whole extraction.
Existing directories that match a directory member are merged without prompting.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-C " dir\fR, \fB\-\-directory " dir
Change to
.I dir
before extracting. A relative
.I archive
path is resolved before the directory change.
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-force
Overwrite existing files without prompting.
.TP
.B \-n, \-\-no\-clobber
Never overwrite; skip members whose paths already exist.
.TP
.B \-i, \-\-interactive
Always prompt before overwrite (requires a tty; non-tty conflicts still abort).
.TP
.B \-p, \-\-preserve
Restore full mode bits, ACLs, and file flags (in addition to the default mtime).
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
List members as they are unpacked (and skipped, when applicable).
.TP
.B \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Display help message and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-
End of options; following arguments are operands (needed for archives whose
names begin with
.BR \- ).
.PP
Only one of
.BR \-f ,
.BR \-n ,
or
.B \-i
may be specified.
.SH SUPPORTED FORMATS
Anything
.B libarchive
can read with
.B archive_read_support_format_all
plus a controlled
.B archive_read_support_format_raw
fallback when the first header is not recognized
(needed for single-file compressed streams such as
.BR .gz / .xz / .zstd ;
raw is omitted from
.BR support_format_all ,
and enabling it together with all formats can mis-bid)
and
.B archive_read_support_filter_all
on the build host, typically including tar (with gzip, xz, bzip2, zstd,
lz4, lzip, lzop, brotli when available), zip, 7z, cpio, and common
single-file compression streams.
.PP
For RAW streams, the member is often named
.B data
internally; unpack renames it by stripping only a simple outer compression
suffix from the archive basename
.RB ( .gz , .bz2 , .xz , .zst , …),
so
.B foo.tar.gz
becomes
.B foo.tar
(not
.BR foo ).
If
.B format_all
had recognized a container archive, unpack would not use the RAW path.
.PP
Exact coverage depends on how
.B libarchive
was built (optional codecs).
.SH EXAMPLES
Extract a gzip-compressed tarball:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ unpack backup.tar.gz
.fi
.RE
.PP
Extract into a directory, forcing overwrite:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ unpack \-C /tmp/out \-f project.zip
.fi
.RE
.PP
Extract without clobbering existing files:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ unpack \-n data.7z
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (no output unless
.B \-v
was given).
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred (file not found, unsafe path, secure-symlink refusal,
unsupported or corrupt archive, I/O failure).
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.B unpack
links against
.BR libarchive (3).
Build requires the libarchive development package and
.BR pkg-config (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pack (1),
.BR extract (1),
.BR libarchive (3)
